    "subject_name": "Mathematics",
    "chapter_id": "6160253f32f74d11258840f1",
    "chapter_name": "Ellipse",
    "year": "2021",
    "shift": "shift_2"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> be an ellipse whose axes are parallel to the co-ordinates axes, having its centre&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;one focus at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and one vertex at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is a tangent to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that,&nbsp;If the standard ellipse is shifted to have center&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then it&#39;s equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>The center is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />The vertices on the major axis are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />The foci are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The&nbsp;eccentricity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0052_7b65cec5ce33.png\" style=\"width: 282px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p>Clearly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>We know that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, equation of ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Intersecting with given tangent</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(as it is tangent)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>18</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
}